From 75a49cc93a37a8015a341056f93253dbb1732e56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:32:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 110/111] Rewrite only the changed instances of the OptiX top
 level structure

When only a few objects changed since the previous top level build (no
geometry other than lights changed, no object added, removed or reordered,
no bottom level structure built or refitted), the OptiX device keeps the
instance and motion transform buffers of the previous build, rewrites the
instances and motion transforms of the changed objects and uploads only
those ranges before building the top level structure again. With no
instance rewritten the previous structure is kept. Object bounds are
computed only for the changed objects in that case.

A change list is trusted only when every object written before it reached
a completed geometry update: ObjectManager::top_level_pending is set
whenever objects other than lights are updated and cleared only at the end
of a GeometryManager::device_update that completed without cancel or error.
Every early return in between (Scene::device_update after the object and
particle updates; the geometry manager on cancel in preprocessing,
attributes, displacement, curve shadow transparency, bottom level builds,
bounds, the top level build or the copies after it; a verification error)
leaves it set, and the next update builds every instance and bound.
A progress cancel during a scene update comes, in Houdini sessions with
persistent updates, only from stopping or closing the session
(RenderSession::cancel/close), from a failed scene transaction, or from a
path tracing error; a device error ends the update as well.

CYCLES_FULL_TOP_LEVEL_BUILD writes every instance and computes every bound
as before, as a reference. CYCLES_VERIFY_TOP_LEVEL compares the kept
instance and motion transform data, on the host and on every device, and
the bounds with a full rewrite, and reports any difference as an error.
CYCLES_TEST_INTERRUPT_TOP_LEVEL=<name part> is a test hook that ends one
update before the bounds and the top level build, as a cancel does.

Rationale: On large instanced scenes the host preparation of the top level instances (slots, motion sizes, motion and instance uploads) costs about 130 ms per object move, while the build itself is a few milliseconds.
Contract: Instances, motion transforms and bounds are identical to a full rewrite on every device (checked by CYCLES_VERIFY_TOP_LEVEL); any change of slots, child structures or motion transform sizes, and any object update whose top level build did not complete, takes the full path; the instance and motion buffers stay allocated between updates.
Tests: tests/houdini_top_level_incremental_smoke.py
